speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I just want to confirm that the understanding that my hon. friend has is agreeable to us. I have a draft motion that I might read to the House, and perhaps I could speak to it afterwards. I move, seconded by the hon. member for Algoma (Mr. Foster):
That the order be discharged;
That the document entitled "Notices of Motion for the Production of Papers", tabled March 15, 1973 be referred to the Standing Joint Committee on Regulations and other Statutory Instruments;
And that a message be sent to the Senate to acquaint their honours that the said document has been referred to their committee.
